flowchart LR
    %% Business example: an expensive order is routed to human review.
    classDef person fill:#fff7ed,stroke:#c2410c,color:#431407
    classDef system fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#1d4ed8,color:#172554
    classDef decision fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#047857,color:#064e3b
    classDef outcome fill:#f5f3ff,stroke:#6d28d9,color:#2e1065

    Author[Operations or risk analyst]:::person
    Rule["Publish rule revision<br/>rule set order.created,<br/>total gte 1000 emits review"]:::system
    Store[Storefront]:::person
    Event["Order-created event<br/>tenant, order id, total"]:::system
    Evaluate["Evaluate active order rule<br/>first_match mode"]:::decision
    High{"Order total<br/>over 1000?"}:::decision
    Approve["No effects, execution completes"]:::outcome
    Review["Effect emitted to topic<br/>orders.review with reason"]:::outcome
    Outbox[("outbox_effects<br/>committed with the execution")]:::outcome
    Workflow["Approval workflow consumes<br/>the review topic"]:::person
    Analyst[Review team]:::person
    Result["Approve or decline order"]:::outcome

    Author --> Rule
    Store --> Event --> Evaluate --> High
    High -->|No| Approve
    High -->|Yes| Review --> Outbox --> Workflow --> Analyst --> Result
    Rule -.->|becomes the active revision| Evaluate
    Review -.->|effect id is stable across retries| Workflow

    Note["Example only: the rule engine decides and emits work.<br/>The external workflow owns the human approval process.<br/>Decision hash and pinned revision make the call auditable."]:::system
